On 2007-11-11, George Gibb wrote:
> Knights, Cavemen,and Samauri seem a lot like Barbs and Valks, but I 
> guess I could try em, they seem a bit boring though.  Is there anything 
> to differentiate them?

Vanilla Cavemen are notoriously dull. Kni and Sam may seem quite similar,
but there are differences. Both are tough melee fighters from the start,
both have codes of conduct (with mostly negligible consequences if you
break them). The Sam starts with a yumi and ya, and a multishot bonus for
those, so you've got ranged combat covered for the start. The knight has a
mount, a lance that you can apply from two spaces away, and can jump. Also,
later on knights are better spellcasters, especially with the quest
artifact when casting attack spells. If you're good at keeping pets, you
might find a mounted knight more interesting than the fairly standard
gameplay of the samurai.

